  "title": "The Net Staked Amount Is Incorrectly Calculated",
  "body": "# The Net Staked Amount Is Incorrectly Calculated\n\n## Finding Description and Impact\n\nIn the `StakingManager::stake` function, when the `stakingLimit` is greater than zero, the following condition must be respected:\n\n```\nnetStaked + msg.value <= stakingLimit\n```\n\nHowever, the `netStaked` is currently computed as:\n\n```\nnetStaked = totalStaked + rewardsAmount - totalClaimed\n```\n\nThis calculation omits the `totalSlashed` value, which represents funds lost due to validator slashing. As a result, the contract may incorrectly assume that more funds are staked than actually available, causing the `stake` function to revert, even for valid stake amounts.\n\n- **Likelihood**: Medium – This miscalculation becomes critical in scenarios where validators have been slashed.\n- **Impact**: High – This can result in a denial of service of the staking function, preventing new users from staking.\n\n## Recommended Mitigation\n\nInclude the slashed amount in the `netStaked` calculation to ensure accuracy:\n\n```diff\nfunction stake() public payable nonReentrant whenNotPaused whenStakingNotPaused {\n    // Check whitelist if enabled\n    if (whitelistEnabled) {\n        require(isWhitelisted(msg.sender), \"Address not whitelisted\");\n    }\n\n    // Validate stake amount\n    require(msg.value >= minStakeAmount, \"Stake amount below minimum\");\n    if (maxStakeAmount > 0) {\n        require(msg.value <= maxStakeAmount, \"Stake amount above maximum\");\n    }\n\n    if (stakingLimit > 0) {\n        // Include rewards and slashing in net stake calculation\n        uint256 rewardsAmount = validatorManager.totalRewards();\n+       uint256 slashingAmount = validatorManager.totalSlashing();\n+       uint256 netStaked = totalStaked + rewardsAmount - totalClaimed - slashingAmount;\n        require(netStaked + msg.value <= stakingLimit, \"Staking limit reached\");\n    }\n\n    totalStaked += msg.value;\n\n    // Convert HYPE to kHYPE amount using exchange ratio\n    uint256 kHYPEAmount = stakingAccountant.HYPEToKHYPE(msg.value);\n\n    // Mint kHYPE tokens based on the conversion\n    kHYPE.mint(msg.sender, kHYPEAmount);\n\n    _distributeStake(msg.value, OperationType.UserDeposit);\n\n    stakingAccountant.recordStake(msg.value);\n\n    emit StakeReceived(address(this), msg.sender, msg.value);\n}\n```",
